"parameter-lang" = "en";

/* Corrections de fautes de frappe des clés anglaises (la clé s'affiche telle quelle sinon) */
"UDP flooding sends packets asynchronously to UDP port 8888 of the target at a maximum rate, but many packets can be lost at software, hardware or network layers. Note that the throughput that is displayed on this chart is the one achieved at the software layer of your device. Therefore, it certainly is above the one at which data is sent over the network: you must use a tool to estimate the reached bandwitdh. Either sniff the network or count packets on the target, for instance." = "UDP flooding sends packets asynchronously to UDP port 8888 of the target at a maximum rate, but many packets can be lost at software, hardware or network layers. Note that the throughput that is displayed on this chart is the one achieved at the software layer of your device. Therefore, it certainly is above the one at which data is sent over the network: you must use a tool to estimate the reached bandwidth. Either sniff the network or count packets on the target, for instance.";
"Click on your prefered blinking rectangle to choose between advanced interface, step-by-step heatmap and documentation. Click on the question marks to get help about each interface." = "Click on your preferred blinking rectangle to choose between advanced interface, step-by-step heatmap and documentation. Click on the question marks to get help about each interface.";
"Parallel TCP connections will be established to %@ on TCP ports from 1 to 65535, to find open services. The new discovered services will be displayed on the bottom view. You can interrupt this task by pressing the STOP button." = "Parallel TCP connections will be established to %@ on TCP ports 1 to 65535 to find open services. Newly discovered services will be displayed in the bottom view. You can interrupt this task by pressing the STOP button.";
"A TCP connection to the Discard port (9/TCP) of %@ will be established. Data will then be sent on this connection at the maximum throughput available, by this device to this target host, to evaluate the maximum speed that can be reached in the outgoing direction. You can interrupt this task by pressing the STOP button." = "A TCP connection will be established to the Discard port (9/TCP) of %@. This device will then send data to the target host over this connection at the maximum available throughput, to evaluate the maximum speed that can be reached in the outgoing direction. You can interrupt this task by pressing the STOP button.";
"A TCP connection to the Chargen port (19/TCP) of %@ will be established. Data will then be received on this connection at the maximum throughput available, by this device from this target host, to evaluate the maximum speed that can be reached in the incoming direction. You can interrupt this task by pressing the STOP button." = "A TCP connection will be established to the Chargen port (19/TCP) of %@. This device will then receive data from the target host over this connection at the maximum available throughput, to evaluate the maximum speed that can be reached in the incoming direction. You can interrupt this task by pressing the STOP button.";
"ICMP packets of type ECHO_REQUEST will be sent to %@ at a rate of one packet per second. The target should reply with an ICMP packet of type ECHO_REPLY. The round trip type is computed and displayed on the chart. You can interrupt this task by pressing the STOP button." = "ICMP packets of type ECHO_REQUEST will be sent to %@ at a rate of one packet per second. The target should reply with an ICMP packet of type ECHO_REPLY. The round-trip time is computed and displayed on the chart. You can interrupt this task by pressing the STOP button.";
